kpi Stage 3 | 5200 MW | 100% of supply | bad

## When to use
Use this runbook when the day-ahead forecast or live demand reaches 92% of available supply (4784 MW of 5200 MW).

!! A stage is declared by the Duty Director, never by a single operator.

## Stages
### Stage 1: 92% of supply (4784 MW)
- Send a conservation alert by text and app to 380,000 customers.
- Ask large industrial customers on interruptible contracts to be ready to reduce load on 30 minutes of notice.
- Confirm that standby generation at 3 peaking plants can start within 20 minutes.

### Stage 2: 97% of supply (5044 MW)
- Call the demand response program, which delivers about 210 MW.
- Start buying emergency imports from the neighboring utility.
- Brief the regulator by phone.

### Stage 3: 100% of supply (5200 MW)
- Begin rotating outages in blocks A to L, in order. Each block is off for at most 60 minutes.
- Never repeat a block before all twelve have been used.

## Steps for rotating outages
1. Get approval.
-- a) The Duty Director approves in the log.
-- b) The regulator is told within 30 minutes.
2. Protect critical sites.
-- a) Confirm that hospitals, the 911 center and water pumping stations are excluded.
-- b) Check that the exclusion list was updated this month.
3. Run the blocks.
-- a) Open the first block's feeders.
-- b) Restore it after 60 minutes at most, and open the next block.
-- c) Update the public outage map every 15 minutes.
4. Stand down.
-- a) End rotating outages when demand stays below 95% for 60 minutes.
-- b) Restore all blocks.
-- c) File the event report within 24 hours.

!!! Hospitals, the 911 center and water pumping stations must never be switched off.

